{"name":"Where Buffalo Roam","hex":"#c19851","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"where","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["In, at or to what place.","In what situation."]},{"part":"Conjunction","definitions":["While on the contrary; although; whereas.","That."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/where"},{"term":"buffalo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An animal from the subtribe Bubalina, also known as true buffalos, such as the Cape buffalo, Syncerus caffer, or the water buffalo, Bubalus bubalis.","A related North American animal, the American bison, Bison bison."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hunt buffalo.","To outwit, confuse, deceive, or intimidate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/buffalo"},{"term":"roam","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To wander or travel freely and with no specific destination.","To range or wander over."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of roaming; a wander; a travel without aim or destination"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roam"}],"entries":[{"title":"Roam","blocks":[{"text":"\"Roam\" is a song by American new wave band the B-52's released as the third single from their fifth studio album, Cosmic Thing (1989). The vocals are sung by Kate Pierson and Cindy Wilson. The B-52's worked with a co-writer, Robert Waldrop, who penned the lyrics. Released as a single in 1989, \"Roam\" peaked at number three on the US Billboard Hot 100 and entered the top 10 in Canada, Ireland, and New Zealand."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/75/Roam_%28The_B-52%27s_single_-_cover_art%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roam","wikidata":"Q7339722"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/75/Roam_%28The_B-52%27s_single_-_cover_art%29.jpg/250px-Roam_%28The_B-52%27s_single_-_cover_art%29.jpg?utm_source=en.